{"t":"2026-10-22T15:33:49.622Z","event":"finish","launch":"0101-cm-cs","n":2,"role":"cm-cs","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":42730,"cumulative":203801,"cost":0.4027,"turns":5,"minutes":0.66,"sessions":[],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I delegated all five orders to `demo-builder` with a 150000 budget each, and each command returned without error.\n\n| Order | Lesson | Builder | Messages |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| O-1 | one-share-tells-nothing | demo-builder | M-1, M-14 |\n| O-2 | slow-hash-hurts-guessers | demo-builder | M-2, M-15 |\n| O-3 | drivers-stop-switching | demo-builder | M-3, M-17 |\n| O-4 | eight-cores-not-eight-times | demo-builder | M-4, M-18 |\n| O-5 | faster-link-same-wait | demo-builder | M-5, M-19 |\n\nWhere I was unsure:\n- **Only one builder to split across.** You asked me to split the orders across my builders, but the org has a single builder role, `demo-builder` (also delegated by cm-math), so everything went to it. Up to three of its sessions can run at once, so the orders should still be built in parallel. I couldn't group related lessons by session; that would need several builder ids.\n- **No `--after` links.** None of these orders came back marked as depending on another, so they're all ready to build now.\n- **Builds may be held.** Builder sessions only launch once `dispatch-check --kind=build` passes, which means the WBR, retro and founder digest come first. Eight ritual orders (O-6 to O-13) are still in their run stage, so the builds may wait until those are held.\n- **Two messages per order.** Each delegation produced a pair of messages, and the numbering skips M-16. I took the gap to be a message created somewhere else and didn't look into it."}
