{"t":"2026-10-22T15:42:58.242Z","event":"finish","launch":"0267-chief-of-staff","n":5,"role":"chief-of-staff","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":108277,"cumulative":1883913,"cost":1.2838,"turns":22,"minutes":4.96,"sessions":["S-4"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I handled two items and the session is now closed because the queue is empty.\n\n**1. RITUAL-design-review-202610221532 (O-8, check stage): pass.** I checked the head-of-product's design-review record against the repo:\n- The 13 lessons it covers, their versions and their `go` decisions all match the 13 launch-review records from 2026-10-22.\n- Its finding counts add up to 13.\n- It has a Decision section, and the stand-in line and every chair objection are carried.\n\nI added three objections, all carried, to its Objections section and changed nothing else:\n- The trigger also named \"a new incident\", and the record never identifies it.\n- The open layout and told-not-shown lessons from the 2026-10-14 review were not re-checked.\n- Its board asks are addressed to the chief of staff, who doesn't write `board.json` in this run, so they go to the handoff.\n\n**2. RITUAL-vertical-review-202610221532 (O-10, run stage, I chaired): done, now waiting for head-of-product's check.** I filled the record at `company/rituals/records/2026-10-22-vertical-review.md` from:\n- the coverage, metrics and overlap command outputs;\n- the founder events and the releases, board and founder-inbox files;\n- the vertical strategy docs.\n\nThe main picture:\n- Five newer categories hold 433 lessons on disk but have published only 12.\n- History (259%), behavioral economics (157%) and Life Hacks engine-v2 (103%) are over budget and at STOP.\n- There is no learner data yet, because no learner events are stored (W-706 is still backlog).\n\nThe verdicts: NCM keep; History fix; behavioral economics fix; Books pause; Big Ideas keep at pilot; Life Hacks fix; Exam prep stays proposed; no new vertical. The record names five objections: two are answered and three are carried, one of them the stand-in line.\n\n**Things that confused me:**\n- `company/rituals/templates/design-review.md`, listed among my read paths, doesn't exist. The accept text does say the company has no template for this ritual.\n- The vertical-review scaffold puts `## 4. Objections` before `## Decision`, while the accept text describes the record as ending with Decision and then Objections. I kept the scaffold's order, and code accepted it when I left.\n- The vertical-review \"asks\" step expects board items, but in this run I can't write `board.json`, so I listed the asks in the record for the handoff to file.\n- The board uses a `state` field, not `status`."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T15:43:09.914Z","event":"guard","launch":"0333-demo-builder","n":8,"role":"demo-builder","via":"hook","tool":"Bash","rule":"bash","why":"`<a command the guard cannot read>`: the guard cannot read this line, so it refuses it. To write a file, use the Write tool (not a shell heredoc or redirect); otherwise spell the command out in plain words (no $(…), `…` or variable as a command, git subcommand or script name)","detail":"cd /home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-drivers-stop-switching/src/demos/cs/drivers-stop-switching && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Demo.tsx'\nsrc=open(p).read()\nold=src[src.index('      {({ locked }) => ('):src.index('    </Lesson>')]\nnew='''      {({ locked }) => (\n        <Milestones interact={i"}
{"t":"2026-10-22T15:43:16.896Z","event":"finish","launch":"0233-analytics-steward","n":4,"role":"analytics-steward","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":81918,"cumulative":811125,"cost":0.759,"turns":11,"minutes":6.88,"sessions":["S-3"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I checked the 2026-10-22 WBR record (order O-7, RITUAL-wbr-202610221532) and passed it. It moves on to ship, and the session then closed because the queue was empty.\n\n**Why it passed:** the record has a Decision section, and every objection in it is answered or carried. Its numbers agree with the 10-17 WBR: math published went from 75 to 87 and CS from 141 to 142, which matches the 13 lessons published through Meta on 10-22.\n\n**Defects I added as objections, all carried with an owner:**\n1. **QA row compares unlike numbers:** \"this week\" is a pass count (985 of 1,634), but the metric and \"last week\" are a failure count (0 of 1,283). It should report failures, passes and untested separately. Owner: analytics-steward.\n2. **Section 4 units are unclear:** cm-math says \"90 of 97 published\", but the snapshot says 94/99 concepts and 87 published. No line in section 4 says whether it counts lessons or concepts. Owner: chief-of-staff.\n3. **A1 drops one of last week's anomalies:** it follows six of the eight 10-17 anomalies. Untriaged growth (W-1673) is missing, and that count has gone from 737 to 947. Owner: portfolio-manager.\n4. **A3 rework recount is underspecified:** it has to separate text-only version bumps, the first builds of the 351 new lessons, and real rebuilds after review. Owner: analytics-steward.\n5. **Formatting:** section 2 keeps the template's empty table header, so it shows two tables and the first has no rows. Owner: chief-of-staff.\n\n**What confused me:** my first hand-in was refused as \"changed outside its Objections section\", even though I had only appended to the closing `## Objections`. The cause is a bug in `adapters/s3c/rituals.mjs`: its Objections pattern picks the first heading containing \"Objections\". In the WBR template that is `## 6. Objections carried into this week`, so code treats only section 6 as the attendee's part. I moved my objections into section 6's table as rows marked \"raised at check by analytics-steward\", and the check accepted them. I put the bug in `--learned`. Until the pattern is changed to target the closing `## Objections` heading, every WBR check will hit the same refusal."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T15:45:57.542Z","event":"guard","launch":"0193-head-of-product","n":3,"role":"head-of-product","via":"hook","tool":"Bash","rule":"bash","why":"`<a command the guard cannot read>`: the guard cannot read this line, so it refuses it. To write a file, use the Write tool (not a shell heredoc or redirect); otherwise spell the command out in plain words (no $(…), `…` or variable as a command, git subcommand or script name)","detail":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='company/rituals/records/2026-10-22-demo-crit.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nW='artifacts/walkthroughs/{s}/sheet.png'\nL=[\n(\"ant-on-a-cube\",\"v2\",\"keep\",\n \"Sheet 07-reveal: the bent green path stays drawn (dashed) on the cube, and the four chips hold 3.00, 2.41, 2.24 and 2.24 m, every number"}
