{"t":"2026-10-22T15:48:44.966Z","event":"finish","launch":"0193-head-of-product","n":3,"role":"head-of-product","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":196301,"cumulative":5352856,"cost":2.9693,"turns":65,"minutes":13.95,"sessions":["S-2"],"abandoned":[],"denials":1,"said":"I handled three items: one check and two ritual records, all now done. The session ended before a fourth item: my last hand-in was saved, but the follow-up wait for the next item failed when the shared state was locked, and I didn't re-enter without a message id.\n\n1. **Founder digest (O-6), check stage: pass.** I compared the chief of staff's record with `company/ops/progress.md` and the 13 launch-review records dated 2026-10-22. The lesson list, the 98 h lateness and the founder asks all hold. I added one objection, carried to release-manager: \"r11 to r19, each … with your approval\" is too broad. r11 and r12 were first recorded as unapproved deploys the founder accepted afterwards, then reused as id aliases, and the digest says nothing about r12 to r14.\n\n2. **Design review (O-8), as chair standing in for design-lead: passed to check.**\n   - Scope was the 13 lessons published through Meta. None uses a new format.\n   - Main findings:\n     - In slice-a-corner-off, Reset empties the picture the reveal talks about.\n     - In two-corners-off-the-board, the suggested \"Another try\" path never shows the impossible board resisting a retry.\n     - The kit stage is still vertically centred, and the board item to measure that fix (W-827) is still in backlog.\n   - No walkthrough artifacts existed on disk, so this review was not artifact-first. Its findings come second hand from the learner and QA reviews, and the record carries that as an objection.\n\n3. **Demo crit (O-9), as chair: shipped.**\n   - I rebuilt the app in the worktree (about 3 minutes) and recorded fresh walkthroughs of all 13 lessons, then read every contact sheet.\n   - **Keep (8):** ant-on-a-cube, four-cards-one-rule, friends-of-friends-overlap, not-every-circle-is-red, one-link-back-grows-the-core, pick-two-or-pick-four, regions-from-circle-points, two-corners-off-the-board.\n   - **Revise (5):** new-friend-loosens-the-circle, one-metre-more-rope, push-the-frame-over, slice-a-corner-off, three-sticks-one-triangle. Each opens its reveal on the reset state, so the stage contradicts the numbers the reveal quotes. For example, one-metre-more-rope shows \"gap 0.0 cm\" while the reveal says the rope lifted 15.9 cm. That breaks the `formats.md:24` rule (\"No reset that empties it\").\n   - The revise orders belong to the earlier run, so code passes them to the chief of staff. None of the five is fatal, and they stay published until revised versions pass.\n\n**What confused me:**\n- `company/rituals/templates/founder-digest.md` doesn't exist, even though the brief names it.\n- Walkthrough artifacts aren't kept after a lesson ships, yet both the design review and the crit require reading them first.\n- The build changed `tsconfig.json` and `src/data/editorial-profiles.account.json` in the worktree. I reverted both so the record stayed the only changed file.\n- The kernel's state lock refused my hand-in three times. The fourth try said \"run R-7 not running\" because one of the refused calls had in fact gone through. It looked like a failure, but the order had shipped, and its worktree was deleted while I was still in it."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T15:48:58.101Z","event":"finish","launch":"0437-chief-of-staff","n":9,"role":"chief-of-staff","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":82411,"cumulative":808567,"cost":0.6809,"turns":11,"minutes":2.34,"sessions":["S-8"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I reviewed one item. It passed and has shipped, but the session ended before I could pick up a second.\n\n**RITUAL-demo-crit-202610221532 (O-9), check stage: pass.** The chair's Demo Crit record (`company/rituals/records/2026-10-22-demo-crit.md`) meets the template:\n- It judges 13 lessons: 8 keep, 5 revise, none killed. Each lesson has its full section, and the decision table has one row per lesson.\n- All five revises have the same cause. The reveal opens on the state left after Reset, so the picture no longer matches the numbers the reveal quotes (`formats.md:24`).\n- The record names a version and a `go` for each lesson. I checked both against the 13 launch records dated 2026-10-22, and they all match.\n- Every objection has an answer or is carried.\n\nI added two objections of my own to the Objections section and changed nothing else:\n1. Only the chair wrote evaluator findings. The pedagogy-critic, qa-tester and accessibility-reviewer, whom the template lists to report first, gave none. I carried this alongside the chair's own objection, so a pedagogy-critic pass gets weighed before the revisions are built.\n2. The five revised lessons have no order in this run, because they shipped under meta/m6. I answered it: code passes each one to the chief of staff, and the lessons stay published until a revised version passes.\n\n**What confused me:**\n- `room next` twice returned \"state is locked by another process\", and a retry then said \"HARD: run R-13 not running\". `flow show O-9` shows the hand-in had in fact gone through on the first attempt: check pass by chief-of-staff, then ship pass by code, stage `done`. So the leave succeeded, but the lock error hid it and no next item came through. I stopped there.\n- I only had read access to records, templates, triggers and progress. I couldn't check the walkthroughs, the QA and learner reviews, or `formats.md:24` directly, so for those I relied on the launch records."}
